{"content":[{"c":["BAAL-BERITH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Pagan god worshiped in central Canaan around the city of Shechem (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.9.1-4,44-46","r":"Judg.9.1-4,44-46","rawR":"Judg.9.1-4,44-46","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.9.1-4,44-46","value":"Judg.9.1-4,44-46"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 9:1-4, 44-46"},"). Baal-berith (“lord of the covenant”) was probably a local form of Baal, the leading Canaanite fertility god. During the period of the judges, the people of Israel turned from the Lord to worship the idols Baal and Baal-berith (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.8.33","r":"Judg.8.33","rawR":"Judg.8.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.8.33","value":"Judg.8.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 8:33"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=CanaaniteDeitiesandReligion_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"CanaaniteDeitiesandReligion_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"CanaaniteDeitiesandReligion_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Canaanite Deities and Religion"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BaalBerith","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jgs 9:1-4, 44-46","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.9.1-4,44-46","rawQueryValue":"Judg.9.1-4,44-46","sourceRefExact":"Judg.9.1-4,44-46"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 8:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.8.33","rawQueryValue":"Judg.8.33","sourceRefExact":"Judg.8.33"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"067ffc2abe41638561c7a379b9e42a8ba09598dadf23ba482cd7584cb576407c","sourceItemName":"BaalBerith","sourceItemOrder":7,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BaalBerith","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Baal-Berith","title":"Baa